    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 2 USER]\ne011\tI do not think this is fear of finishing.\ne012\tThe ending makes our main participant sound more certain about leaving her town than she was.\ne013\tWe did not fabricate anything, but Jonah used her strongest lines together and removed hesitation.\ne014\tHe says the whole piece compresses time and that the uncertainty is clear earlier.\ne015\tI feel responsible because I conducted the interviews.\ne016\tThis is not just my taste about pacing.\n[Turn 2 ASSISTANT]\ne017\tThat changes the priority.\ne018\tIf the edit alters how a participant's position is understood, you need to review it against the full interview and the promises you made her, not only against dramatic effect.\ne019\tYou and Jonah may still disagree about how much hesitation belongs in the ending, but the disagreement should be grounded in representation.\ne020\tA focused re-edit of that thread could be necessary even if the larger structure remains.",
