    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": false,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 1 USER]\ne001\tMy friend Jonah and I have spent eighteen months making an audio documentary.\ne002\tWe were invited to premiere it at a respected local showcase in six weeks.\ne003\tI produced the reporting and interviews; he built the sound and structure.\ne004\tAfter listening to the latest cut, I think the final third needs a major re-edit.\ne005\tJonah thinks we should finish what we have and learn from an audience.\ne006\tWe are also avoiding a conversation about whether the credit should simply say “by both of us” or name our roles.\n[Turn 1 ASSISTANT]\ne007\tThe edit and credit issues are related because both ask how your different contributions translate into authority.\ne008\tSix weeks may be enough for targeted revision but not for rebuilding the final third without sacrificing the rest.\ne009\tBefore deciding, identify what problem you hear: factual confusion, emotional shape, pacing, or discomfort that the piece is becoming final.\ne010\tOn credit, naming roles can recognize distinct work, but it should not become a substitute for agreeing who decides what.",
